---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-01/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/03-01/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/03-01/',way='https://nfab.eng.wayne.edu/_resources/images/bjd.jpg',tech='https://mnfu.technion.ac.il/e-beam-evaporator-airco-temescal-bjd-1800/';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(6)):String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Temescal BJD-1800 passive witness station" subtitle="" description="Inspect the instrument silhouette and compare an inert disc's off-instrument ideal optical shadow ruler." wide={true}>
<article id="witness" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-01/">← Equipment 03-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#witness-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">03-01 / Temescal BJD-1800 / Passive witness station</p><h2>Temescal BJD-1800</h2><p>Place an inert disc in a representative six-pocket carrier, then read a separate ideal optical shadow worksheet. The ready example shadows 4 of 16 cells, a span of 100 μm. Nothing is deposited or powered.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the silhouette and carrier</h3><div id="witness-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Carrier','Rack'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="witness-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="witness-model" aria-label="Orbitable bench, cosmetic cabinet and removable display cover above six inert wafer pockets"></canvas><p id="witness-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the raised display cover or a pocket to inspect it. The plate outside the chamber reads the optical worksheet. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. The rack is decorative.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Compare an inert witness</h3><div class="e-row"><button id="witness-cover" type="button">Lift visual cover</button><button id="witness-seat" type="button">Seat inert witness</button><button id="witness-example" class="e-run" type="button">Seat and check example</button></div>
<form id="witness-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields"><label>Witness ID<input name="sampleId" value="inert-disc-01" maxlength="96"/></label><label>Disc Ø (mm)<input name="diameterMm" type="number" min="50" max="120" step="any" value="100"/></label>
<label>Pocket<select name="pocket">{[1,2,3,4,5,6].map(n=><option value={n}>P{n}</option>)}</select></label><label>Worksheet light angle from normal<select name="angleDeg">{[0,45,60].map(i=><option value={i} selected={i===45}>{i}°</option>)}</select></label></div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="witness-read" class="e-run" type="submit">Read optical shadow</button><button id="witness-reset" type="button">Reset station</button></div></form><p id="witness-status" role="status">Visual cover down. No witness seated.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read the light-shadow profile</h3><p id="witness-result" role="status">No optical comparison yet.</p><div id="witness-map" aria-label="Shaded and lit positions across sixteen 25-micrometer optical cells"></div><div class="e-row"><button id="witness-json" disabled>Optical geometry JSON</button></div><p>Dark cells indicate geometric occlusion. Light cells indicate ideal unobstructed rays. The grade is visibility, not a measurement or a thickness map. <a href={a+'example-shadow.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Configuration and sources</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original BJD-1800 enclosure and rack visual"/><figcaption>Original cabinet and top-mounted cover, informed by <a href={way}>Wayne State nFab’s BJD-1800 photograph</a>. Exterior dimensions are inferred.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original six-position inert wafer carrier illustration"/><figcaption>Original six-position witness card, based on the count and nominal 4-inch family documented in <a href={tech}>Technion’s BJD-1800 facility record</a>. Both installations belong to the same model family but are not asserted to have identical fixtures.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>The inert design disc is 100 mm nominal. Recess diameter is an original 104 mm, giving 2 mm nominal clearance per side. The enclosure and mechanical travel are visual design estimates, not specifications or reconstructed internals. The case excludes the actual source, vacuum, utilities, thickness monitor and material processing.</p></section>
<section><h3>Geometry and limits</h3><p>For a 100 μm ideal vertical step in a separate optics worksheet, projected shadow is <em>h</em> tan <em>θ</em> where <em>θ</em> is a worksheet light angle measured from the normal. A 16-cell one-dimensional transect uses 25 μm spacing and classifies each cell midpoint. Its raster uncertainty is at most one cell for these preset cases. At 0° there is no projected length. No material, device input, dose or generation of a deposited layer is modeled. This checks the geometric analogy in the register, not a deposition acceptance test.</p></section>
<section id="witness-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'bjd-1800-witness.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Interaction targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives, optional WebXR; physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-01/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#witness header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#witness h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#witness section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#witness button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#witness button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#witness-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#witness-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#witness table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#witness td,#witness th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#witness figure{margin:0}#witness img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#witness caption{text-align:left}#witness input,#witness select,#witness button{min-width:0}#witness .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#witness-map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(16,minmax(0,1fr));max-width:36rem;margin:.65rem 0}#witness-map span{height:2.1rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}</style>
